+# Epic RC4 Context: Landlord Reference Panel & Workflow
+
+<!-- Compiled from planning artifacts. Edit freely. Regenerate with compile-epic-context if planning docs change. -->
+
+## Goal
+
+Give the landlord a per-application reference-checking control surface: a panel that shows every reference's lifecycle state with honest framing, the completed-reference summary, and row actions (start early, skip, take over manually, correct contact details, substitute a referee) so automation never traps the landlord and a dead end always has a next step. RC4.1 shipped the payload contract, RC4.2 rendered it, RC4.3 wires the row actions, RC4.4 completes the attempt-log timeline + notification coverage.
+
+## Stories
+
+- RC4.1: Detail payload extension (`reference_calls[]` + hooks + disclaimers) — done (#604)
+- RC4.2: Reference panel (status & summary) — done (#605)
+- RC4.3: Row actions — start, skip, take over, correct, substitute (THIS story)
+- RC4.4: Attempt log, export & notification completeness
+
+## Requirements & Constraints
+
+- Row actions are hidden entirely in the Off (attestation declined) state; the feature is off for that application.
+- "Start this check now" asks once inline (never a modal) and starts via the RC2.3 start API (optional `?slot=` variant pre-declared for when the per-row UI demands it).
+- "Take over manually" (waiting states + unreachable): inline confirmation; on confirm the row gets `taken_over_at`, the sweep stops sending, referee chips + attempt-log export render inline, label "You're handling this one"; the form link stays live and a late completion still transitions to `form_completed`, updates the panel, and notifies (§8.6).
+- Correction (awaiting_correction rows): inline edit-trio, "Save & resend" is audit-logged, writes corrected_email/corrected_phone (snapshot immutable), updates the application trio, sets correction_cycles = 1, re-queues (queued, next_attempt_at = now()). Second failure → unreachable + referee_contact_invalid fraud signal (stamped only on exhaustion — never fabricated).
+- Substitution (terminal objected/unreachable, can_substitute_referee): same inline edit captures the NEW trio; a NEW reference_call row for the slot (prior row retained as history); audit entry carries old + new row ids.
+- Every action endpoint is ownership-checked and guarded on the row's expected pre-state (AD-14 single-UPDATE guards, 0-row = stand down).
+
+## Technical Decisions
+
+- One live row per (application, slot, owner) via partial unique index — terminal rows don't occupy the slot, so substitution inserts freely; a skipped row does occupy it until re-enabled.
+- The sweep (RC3.5) owns every send; creation (incl. substitution rows) sets next_attempt_at = now() and sends nothing. Sweep SELECT already excludes taken_over_at IS NOT NULL rows (A7).
+- Effective contact = corrected_* when present, else the immutable contact_* snapshot.
+- AD-7 correction is landlord-driven (A1): no correction_token, no applicant self-serve; the landlord contacts the applicant and edits the trio inline.
+- All transitions obey guarded updates + sticky terminals (AD-14); lifecycle events write audit_log rows (AD-16) — substitution audit carries old + new row ids.
+- rc3-7 provides the referee_contact_invalid stamp mechanism; the LIVE second-failure terminal (awaiting_correction → unreachable) is RC4.3's delivery.
+- Notifications: awaiting_correction is in-app only (rc3-6); unreachable/completed notifications exist; RC4.3's landlord-initiated actions need no new notifications (RC4.4 covers completeness).
+- Additive payload keys only (expand-only, back-compat decoders) — the RC line's contract discipline.
+
+## UX & Interaction Patterns
+
+- Brand pattern: inline confirmations, never modals (§7.4, §7.7).
+- Per-row `⋯` overflow menu: Start this check now / Skip this reference (queued), Start this check (skipped = re-enable), Take over manually (waiting + unreachable), Substitute referee (objected/unreachable per hooks).
+- §8.3 inline edit-trio wireframe (Name/Email/Phone + Save & resend) with the applicant's contact chips below.
+- State label after takeover: "You're handling this one".
+- All copy verbatim from the cited UX sections — no rewriting.
+
+## Cross-Story Dependencies
+
+- Needs RC2.3's start/skip/re-enable APIs (merged), RC3.5's sweep (taken_over_at-aware), rc3-7's stamp_referee_contact_invalid, RC4.1's payload + hooks (can_substitute_referee), RC4.2's panel.
+- RC4.4 inherits the takeover surface (export affordance renders inline here; the full timeline + OQ-5 clipboard toast are RC4.4).
