+## Acceptance Criteria (BDD — from epic RC4.3 + UX §7.4/§7.7/§8.2/§8.3/§8.6 + A1/A7/AD-7/AD-14/AD-16)
+
+**AC1 — Pre-trigger row actions**
+> **Given** a `queued` row, when the landlord opens its `⋯` overflow and chooses "Start this
+> check now", then an inline one-time confirm renders (§7.4 verbatim copy), and confirming
+> starts that slot's check via the RC2.3 start API (`?slot=` — other slots untouched); "Skip
+> this reference" excludes the row (`queued → skipped`, re-enable-able via the Skipped row's
+> "Start this check").
+
+**AC2 — Take over manually**
+> **Given** an in-flight (`queued`/`contact_initiated`) or `unreachable` row, when "Take over
+> manually" is chosen, then the §7.7 inline confirmation renders (never a modal); on confirm
+> the row gets `taken_over_at` — the sweep stops sending (already wired, A7), the referee's
+> effective-contact chips + the attempt-log export render inline, the label reads "You're
+> handling this one" — and the form link stays live: a late completion still transitions to
+> `form_completed`, updates the panel, and notifies (§8.6).
+
+**AC3 — Correction (one cycle)**
+> **Given** an `awaiting_correction` row, when the landlord edits the trio inline (§8.3,
+> applicant contact chips below) and saves, then the change is audit-logged, writes
+> `corrected_email`/`corrected_phone` (+ `corrected_name`; snapshot immutable — A1), updates
+> the application trio, sets `correction_cycles = 1`, and re-queues (`queued`,
+> `next_attempt_at = now()`).
+> **And** a second failure (bounce / SMS failure / wrong-person) converts the row to
+> `unreachable` with the `referee_contact_invalid` signal stamped (AD-7 — the rc3-7 mechanism
+> goes live here).
+
+**AC4 — Substitute referee**
+> **Given** a terminal `objected` or `unreachable` row (`can_substitute_referee`), when the
+> landlord substitutes via the inline edit-trio, then a NEW `reference_call` row is created
+> for the slot (`queued`, `next_attempt_at = now()`, new trio as snapshot) with the prior row
+> retained as history, and the audit entry carries old + new row ids (AD-16).
+
+**AC5 — Guard rails**
+> **Given** any action endpoint, when it runs, then it is ownership-checked (three-UUID +
+> `verify_application_ownership` + archived-vacancy prechecks) and guarded on the row's
+> expected pre-state (AD-14 single-UPDATE; 0-row → branded 409/404, no mutation), and manual
+> actions are hidden entirely in the Off (declined) state (no rows — server suppression +
+> the panel's Off branch).
